WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.333
The flat tool turns the plug. The middle driver runs out of room first and takes the turning load. The front pin still has room to move.

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:03.667
The hook lifts the front pin against its spring. When the hook lowers, the spring pushes both pins back down.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.333
The hook now has to lift the middle driver past the edge pressing against it. That extra resistance tells the picker which pin is binding.

00:00:05.333 --> 00:00:06.042
As the driver clears the shear line, the resistance gives way. The plug turns until the next pin stops it. The picker feels that movement through the turning tool and may hear a click as the parts meet.

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:06.583
Turning pressure keeps the holes slightly out of line. The spring presses the blue driver onto the edge of the plug. The pale key pin drops with the hook. The driver is set.

